Found by the k14 worker and reviewer (2026-11-19), pre-existing, outside k14. App::Briefing::_build_home (lib/App/Briefing.pm, last branch) ends in getpwuid, which Perl does not implement on Win32 (perlport; Win32 config has d_getpwent undef). With HOME, USERPROFILE and HOMEDRIVE+HOMEPATH all unset or empty the CLI dies instead of falling back. Done when the Windows branch never reaches getpwuid and states a clear error or fallback, with a test.

k23 (README/POD) documents App::Briefing's home fallback as HOME; on Windows USERPROFILE, then HOMEDRIVE+HOMEPATH; then the password entry; then the current directory (lib/App/Briefing.pm:86). On Windows the getpwuid step dies first (this card), so the current-directory fallback is not reached there until this is fixed.
